00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:28.140
"When I Put My Hand Up, a Taxi Stopped"

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:28.140
"When I Put My Hand Up, a Taxi Stopped."

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:37.110
Don't you think that Uramichi-<i>san</i>
has been preoccupied all morning?

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.360
Yeah. I wonder if something happened.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.190
Iron... No.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.490
M-Maki***?

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.280
That's not it.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:50.330
His Advice Room segment is coming up next.
Is he gonna be okay like that?

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:53.710
He's normally "not okay,"
so it'll probably be okay.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.710
Macaroni...

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.500
No, not quite right.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.300
"Advice Room"

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.300
Kids!

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.710
"Advice Room"

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.710
Gather around!

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.170
"Advice Room"

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.170
Yay!

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.220
Today, I'll listen to your concerns

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:10.060
and give you advice from my own,
one-sided perspective!

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.520
Which of you has concerns?!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:15.140
--Me! Me, me, me!
--Me! Me! Me! Me...!

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:17.480
All right, then! Kenji-<i>kun</i>. Go ahead!

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:18.400
Okay!

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.190
U-Um... Err...

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.940
Take your time.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.870
I have so much fun every day that
I feel bad for you, Uramichi Oniisan!

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.780
What should I do?!

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.700
Well, don't worry about me.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.160
Please stay the way you are, Kenji-<i>kun</i>.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.460
Okay!

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:40.250
--Okay, who's nex--
--Do you have concerns,
too, Uramichi Oniisan?

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.420
I do. Lately, I've been having problems
remembering the names of things.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.260
--Don't worry!
--Hm?

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:51.140
My mommy is 26 years old, but she
sometimes can't remember people's names.

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.520
It happened the other day, too,
when we went to a supermarket.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.640
"Supermarket Torima"

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:59.270
"Supermarket Torima"

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:59.270
There, we saw a man who was
buying some pickled mackerels,

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:02.570
burdock root, and a lot of alcohol.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:06.530
Me and Mommy thought that
he looked like someone we knew.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.450
She said she couldn't really
remember who he looked like.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:15.410
So, I told her that he looked like
Uramichi Oniisan from <i>Together with Maman</i>!

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:20.130
Then she said, "Uramichi Oniisan
is younger than him."

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.540
O-Oh, yeah?

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.920
Something like that happened, huh?

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.430
But he really looked like you!

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.760
Well, yeah, it <i>was </i>me.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:35.560
That was... probably him.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.690
Uramichi-<i>san </i>likes pickled fish, so...

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.230
--What?
--What?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.980
I didn't say anything.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.940
All right, then! Who's next?!

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.490
Me! Me, me, me!

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.780
Okay, then, Saki-<i>chan</i>!

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:52.240
Is there a kind of food that you like?

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:55.200
Saki-chan. We're doing
Advice Room right now.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.870
Regular questions should--

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.540
Hm?

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.460
What's that thing called again?

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:09.380
Iron... No.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.340
That's not it.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.140
Macaron!

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.680
What?!

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.890
"Whisper... Whisper... Whisper..."
Macarons are his favorite food?

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.140
"Whisper... Whisper... Whisper..."
--Really?
--He doesn't seem like a macaron person.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.560
"Whisper... Whisper... Whisper..."
It's a little creepy.

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:20.890
Uramichi-<i>san</i>!

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:24.860
That was a terrible way of
hiding your love for pickled fish.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.320
What?

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:29.030
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:35.280
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.580
Hello!

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:41.410
I'm feeling relatively calm today.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:45.880
It's because I'll have two
days off starting tomorrow.

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.170
Two days off!

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.920
Uramichi Oniisan! Lift me up high!

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:51.970
Sure!

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.470
Up and up!

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:54.550
--Me, too!
--Me, too!

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:55.510
Up and up!

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:59.350
--I wonder how long it's been
since I had two days off.
--Taxes are up and up!

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:01.180
Two days off!

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:06.440
Why is he in such a good mood?

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:10.030
It couldn't be... that no one
has told him about it, right?

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:11.900
"Together with Maman"

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.110
"Together with Maman"

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.110
Isn't this bad?

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.820
"Together with Maman"

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.820
This is bad.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.080
Good work!

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.580
A company trip?

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:23.960
Y-Yeah.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:30.340
By the way, if you don't go, they'll treat
it as if you're skipping work. Moreover...

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.470
Hey, Uramichi-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:35.300
"-<i>chan</i>"?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:38.220
A company trip! How exciting, huh?

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.930
Um... I wasn't told about--

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:43.690
The bus leaves at 8:00 AM
tomorrow. If you're late,

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:46.060
you'll have to pay for
your own transportation.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:49.150
So don't be late.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:52.650
Yay! I can't wait! I can't wait!

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:54.400
--I can't wait!
--Did you have plans for those
two days off by any chance?

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.410
--Yay! Yay! Yay!
--Did you have plans for those
two days off by any chance?

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.120
I sure as hell did.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:03.080
I planned to rest, which is
more important than anything.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:06.750
"Sat"

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:06.750
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.630
"The Following Morning"

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.260
"Somewhere in Tokyo"

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.760
G'morning!

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:22.560
You're here early despite the fact
that you didn't wanna go.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.310
I have a habit of arriving
ten minutes early, so...

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:26.980
Your voice is so soft.

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.230
Good morning!

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.810
Hm?

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.530
Good morning!

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.280
Morning!

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:37.910
You sports guys pack light
for this kind of event, huh?

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.410
Oh, it may be because
we're used to training camps.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:43.750
Uramichi Oniisan.
Please check out this T-shirt!

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.040
It's cute, isn't it?

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:48.630
It's not--

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:52.170
It's not cute! It's so not cute that I
stumbled over the words! I'm in shock!

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:56.260
There's this site where I buy stuff
like food and toys for Sayuri-<i>san</i>.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:59.640
If you buy two of this
T-shirt on that site...

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.810
...they'll give you this!

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:02.810
What's that?

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.350
--It's a pen ca--
--What's that?

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.890
--It's a pen ca--
--What's that?

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.560
It's a pen case.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:11.650
Sorry that I'm late.

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.070
Hm?

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.780
I came running here. Now I feel hot.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:18.070
Is that thing popular
around here or something?

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:20.030
Iketeru gave this to me, so...

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.200
"Vrooom"

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.460
In any case, I haven't been able
to go to a hot spring this year,

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:31.790
so I'm looking forward to it.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.210
Yeah!

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:35.920
Oh, is there any movie that
you recommend, Kuma-<i>san</i>?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:38.470
"Man-Eating Salmon vs. Bunny on a Moped"

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:38.470
Maybe the <i>Man-Eating Salmon </i>series.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:40.090
Is it good?

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.760
No, not at all.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:44.220
I'm planning...

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:47.100
--...to have you two do more new stuff.
--Err...

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.770
I'm counting on you.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.400
Men flourish after 30!

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:56.740
Oh... You look tired today.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:00.240
And your skin! You were
drinking yesterday, weren't you?

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.070
Yes.

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.820
"Hot Spring Inn"
"Hirou-kan"

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.670
Ahh! We're finally here!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.970
--Yay! We're at a hot spring!
--Hot spring! Hot spring!

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.800
Capellini-<i>chan</i>, hurry up!

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:23.050
Wait for me!

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:26.770
Hey. We should follow the women's example
and force ourselves to enjoy this trip.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:28.730
Let's at least pretend to have fun.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:30.980
"Welcome"

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:30.980
"Together with Maman Group"

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:32.980
"Welcome"
"Together with Maman Group"

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:32.980
I wanna go home.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.940
"You can discover wonderful items
that are new to you!"

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.940
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.440
"Gokurou Room"

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:41.030
"Gokurou Room"

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:41.030
Man... I really like tatami!

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:43.530
Ah, should we start a pillow fight?

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.740
No.

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:47.990
People don't usually have a pillow fight
as soon as they arrive in the room.

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:51.370
Ah, I know. They do it before they go
to bed, right? The pillow fight.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:55.460
Well, it's not what adults who're almost
30 would do in the first place.

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:56.380
What?

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:58.340
What?

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:02.180
Don't tell me he's yearning
for a pillow fight...

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:05.350
Oh... Um... Telling each other scary
stories is a typical thing to do

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.970
when staying at an inn, isn't it?

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:09.020
Not gonna happen.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:09.890
What?!

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.940
What?

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:15.400
He wants to hear scary stories, too?

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:19.110
Iketeru-<i>kun</i>. Is it possible that you've
never gone on a school trip?

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:23.530
Ah... Yes. A competition happened
to overlap the trip, so I couldn't.

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:27.910
My family had strict rules, so I couldn't
do sleep overs with my friends, either.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:31.830
So, I've always dreamed
of doing this kind of thing.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:38.630
A-Anyhow, let's go soak in the hot spring!

00:12:38.630 --> 00:12:40.050
Here's your yukata.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:40.670
"Wanna Quit Bunny"

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:45.840
Iketeru-<i>kun</i>. If you like, I can teach you
about all kinds of school trip stuff.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:50.100
Take this opportunity to let me know
about anything you wanna do, okay?

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.390
What?

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:53.480
I'm sorry. I wasn't listening.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:01.530
Ah... An open-air bath is so great.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:04.450
It's so refreshing!

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:07.490
Utano-<i>chan</i>. How's it going
with your boyfriend lately?

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.530
Same as always.

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:12.620
When I told him that I was
leaving for a trip this morning,

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.710
he said, "What about my meals?"

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.420
I was like, "It's only two days.
Figure it out yourself!

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.210
Can't you at least say,
'Have a safe trip!'"

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:24.630
Speaking of which,
your boyfriend is from Osaka, right?

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.010
I like the Kansai accent.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.140
What? It's nothing special.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.390
If you hear it all the time,
you'll start using it yourself.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:33.520
Kayo-<i>chan</i>. If you like the Kansai accent
so much, what about Usahara-<i>kun</i>?

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.230
If I remember correctly, he's from Kyoto.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:38.520
Oh, really? That's kind of unexpected.

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:41.070
Ah, but Usahara-<i>san </i>isn't really...

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:43.110
I like a sincere guy, so...

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:47.280
Oh, yeah... Usahara-<i>kun</i>
isn't a bad person, but...

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:49.780
He is kind of a good-for-nothing.

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:53.910
Women's bath sounds lively.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.960
I wonder what they're talking about.
I wish I could listen in.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:59.380
They're mostly badmouthing
you, Usahara-<i>san</i>.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:01.960
You sure have good ears.
I didn't wanna hear that.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.090
Well, we probably should've
split up for our baths.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:08.680
Everyone's here and
it kind of feels crowded.

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:12.060
It feels like the women went together
and we just followed along.

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:21.190
"Banquet Hall"
"Dakyou-an"

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:21.190
Here. Please.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:24.150
Please take a gulp! Take a gulp!

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:28.070
"Matching Look of Love in Naniwa"
"Yasuko Oide"

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:28.070
Take a gulp!

